{
  "case_id": "2018-18-315",
  "document_hash": "b008a41109cecb41ef6deb458efd907abb7dbdff8d85ac415af8baa9d6f58a65",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-18-315",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b008a41109cecb41ef6deb458efd907abb7dbdff8d85ac415af8baa9d6f58a65",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b008a41109ce-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:31 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Cochise Consultancy, Inc. (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2018-18-315",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b008a41109cecb41ef6deb458efd907abb7dbdff8d85ac415af8baa9d6f58a65",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b008a41109ce-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Eleventh Circuit held that a relator who waited seven years to file suit after witnessing an alleged fraud against the United States Government was entitled to rely on the equitable tolling principle, the discovery rule, that is established by Section 3731(b)(2) of the False Claims Act, even though the government declined to intervene in the suit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2018-18-315",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b008a41109cecb41ef6deb458efd907abb7dbdff8d85ac415af8baa9d6f58a65",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b008a41109ce-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Isn't the United States in some sense a party even if it hasn't intervened? After all, it's going to get the lion's share of the recovery, and, if I understand correctly, it -- the suit can't be dismissed without notice and -- and approval by the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Cochise Consultancy, Inc. (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2018-18-315",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b008a41109cecb41ef6deb458efd907abb7dbdff8d85ac415af8baa9d6f58a65",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b008a41109ce-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BOUTROUS: The government does have certain rights, Your Honor, when it does not intervene, but it is not a party."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-18-315",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b008a41109cecb41ef6deb458efd907abb7dbdff8d85ac415af8baa9d6f58a65",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b008a41109ce-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Does -- does that mean, Mr. Boutrous, that the statute of limitations can change in the middle of the lawsuit if the government decides to intervene?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-18-315",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b008a41109cecb41ef6deb458efd907abb7dbdff8d85ac415af8baa9d6f58a65",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b008a41109ce-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: I mean, this is a -- this is an interesting case because it really does create a statutory interpretation dilemma."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-18-315",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b008a41109cecb41ef6deb458efd907abb7dbdff8d85ac415af8baa9d6f58a65",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b008a41109ce-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Where -- where is the ambiguity? I'm not seeing ambiguity. Where exactly is the phrase that you think is ambiguous?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2018-18-315",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b008a41109cecb41ef6deb458efd907abb7dbdff8d85ac415af8baa9d6f58a65",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b008a41109ce-0001-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Approximately 70 percent of qui tam suits are initiated by private relators. The Department of Justice intervenes in only about a fifth of those. But, in every case where the result is successful, either by settlement or by judgment, the United States is the ultimate beneficiary. In every case, the United States gets at least 70 percent of the proceeds."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-315",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b008a41109cecb41ef6deb458efd907abb7dbdff8d85ac415af8baa9d6f58a65",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b008a41109ce-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So why didn't Congress reference that? Why didn't they, instead of just saying official of the United States, say official designated under the subsection you just mentioned?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-18-315",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b008a41109cecb41ef6deb458efd907abb7dbdff8d85ac415af8baa9d6f58a65",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b008a41109ce-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: And what happens if a relator brings a suit, the government chooses not to intervene, but then, as the suit goes on, the -- the -- it -- it appears that the relator is not fulfilling -- is not litigating the case in a -- in a diligent way? What can the government do at that point?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2018-18-315",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b008a41109cecb41ef6deb458efd907abb7dbdff8d85ac415af8baa9d6f58a65",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b008a41109ce-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MAYFIELD: The government always has the ultimate ability to take over the case, Justice Alito. The relator is basically a free agent within those statutory constraints."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2018-18-315",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b008a41109cecb41ef6deb458efd907abb7dbdff8d85ac415af8baa9d6f58a65",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b008a41109ce-0002-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We don't think he deserves the full 30 percent. And the court can knock it down."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-18-315",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b008a41109cecb41ef6deb458efd907abb7dbdff8d85ac415af8baa9d6f58a65",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b008a41109ce-0002-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case was submitted."
    },
